  "searchSummary": {
    "en": "Meta launched Muse, a U.S.-only personal agent that can connect to user-selected services, work across browser and app tasks, and request approval for sensitive actions.",
    "zhHans": "Meta 推出仅限美国的个人智能体 Muse，可连接用户选择的服务，跨浏览器与应用执行任务，并在敏感操作前请求批准。"
  },
  "summary": {
    "en": "Meta launched Muse on September 8 as a U.S. consumer personal agent for web, iOS, Android, and WhatsApp. Meta says the agent, powered by Muse Spark, can work on tasks such as email, travel, forms, and purchases, and can continue work after the user leaves the app. Meta describes a dedicated Muse Secure VM and a separate Sentinel agent intended to gate internet actions and request approval for sensitive steps. Independent coverage confirms the initial U.S. product rollout and identifies trust, privacy, and adoption as unresolved questions.",
    "zhHans": "Meta 于 9 月 8 日将 Muse 作为美国消费者个人智能体推出，覆盖网页、iOS、Android 和 WhatsApp。Meta 称，该智能体由 Muse Spark 驱动，可处理邮件、旅行、表单和购买等任务，并能在用户离开应用后继续工作。Meta 描述了专用 Muse Secure VM 与独立 Sentinel 智能体，旨在审核互联网操作，并在敏感步骤前请求批准。独立报道确认了初始美国产品发布，并将信任、隐私和采用情况列为未解问题。"
  },
  "narrative": {
    "en": "Muse represents a move from Meta's earlier assistant features toward a separate consumer agent that can retain context, use connected services, and initiate actions. Its initial scope is limited to the United States, and Meta's claimed privacy and security properties have not been independently audited in the reviewed sources. TechCrunch notes that the product asks users to connect high-sensitivity services such as email, calendars, payments, health, shopping, and browser-accessed accounts. The event should therefore distinguish an announced, opt-in product architecture from evidence of reliable autonomy, secure implementation, or broad consumer adoption.",
    "zhHans": "Muse 代表 Meta 从此前的助手功能转向一个独立的消费者智能体：它可保留上下文、使用已连接服务并发起操作。其初始范围限于美国，且所审查来源尚未对 Meta 声称的隐私与安全特性进行独立审计。TechCrunch 指出，该产品要求用户连接邮件、日历、支付、健康、购物和通过浏览器访问的账户等高敏感服务。因此，事件应区分已宣布的、选择加入的产品架构，与可靠自主性、安全实现或广泛消费者采用的证据。"
  },
